 = target held base pose == `fixed_pos` (bottom of the hole bore).\n  Hole yaw-only randomized -> hole axis is world +z.  => `dz = peg_z - hole_z` is height above the bore\n  bottom; the bore mouth is at `dz = 0.025`.\n- `success`  <=> xy_dist < 2.5 mm AND dz < 0.04*0.025 = **1.0 mm**.\n- `engaged`  <=> xy_dist < 2.5 mm AND dz < 0.9 *0.025 = **22.5 mm** (i.e. >= 2.5 mm into the bore).\n- `keypoint_distance` = mean over 4 keypoints (offsets -0.075..+0.075 along each frame's z) of\n  || held_kp - target_kp ||. When the peg is upright this is just `norm(peg_position - hole_position)`.\n\n### Reset randomisation (fixed_env.json)\n- hand: hole_tip + [0,0,0.047] +- [0.05, 0.05, 0.02]; yaw +- 90 deg.\n- peg-in-gripper offset +- [6, 3, 6] mm (translation only, in gripper frame) -> **unobservable lateral\n  grasp error up to ~6.7 mm**, vs 0.057 mm clearance. The policy MUST do a contact search.\n- fingertip is 0.0324 m above the peg base => at reset `dz ~ 0.0396 +- 0.026`, `dxy` up to ~0.057.\n\n## Diagnosed flaw in the original reward\nAt the bore mouth (`dz = 25 mm`) the isotropic keypoint distance is dominated by `dz`:\nmoving `dxy` from 20 mm -> 0 changes total reward by only **0.074/step**.  An explicit\n`squash(dxy)` funnel moves the same distance for **0.40/step** (5.5x). At the start height\n(`dz = 47 mm`) the ratio is 12x. So the original reward gives almost no lateral-centering signal\nuntil the peg is already low.\n\n## Reward ceiling accounting (original)\n- hover aligned at mouth (dz 25 mm, dxy 0): 0.42/step\n- fully inserted: 0.917 + 1 + 1 = 2.917/step\n\n## Submission log\n(see ROUNDS.md)\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
