{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCKQNhNcToUpabQLbQao","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01T2gg5RjpW9TDsY54Yy6x3L","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> /workspace/research/ROUNDS.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Round 1 RESULT (agent-1, 2689 s)\n| cand | recipe | score | successes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | baseline + lateral funnel | **0.3936** | 403/1024 |\n| 1 | + ultrafine(600) + gated depth + `success*(1+2*progress)` | 0.3574 | 366/1024 |\n\nBaseline = 0.378 (387). Final-epoch mean episode return from the checkpoint filename:\ncand_0 142.7, cand_1 209.5 (scale only, not comparable across recipes).\n\n**Conclusions**\n- H1 supported but weak (+0.016 ~ 1 SE). The lateral funnel is kept as the base recipe (\"R1A\").\n- H2 refuted (-0.036 vs H1). Most likely culprit: `episode_progress`-weighted success.\n  **Neither the actor obs (13 dims + prev_action) nor the critic state contains time**, so a\n  time-varying reward is not predictable by the value function -> noisy advantages.\n  => RULE: do not make reward magnitude depend on `episode_progress`.\n- Since a 6-11x stronger approach gradient bought only +0.016, the approach phase is *not* the\n  bottleneck. The bottleneck is the "}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":591,"cache_creation_input_tokens":540,"cache_read_input_tokens":212204,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":540},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f43d26ba-365d-4aca-85d2-d7eee3bfb38e","uuid":"51d01a14-bc2d-42e7-bcaa-994087f14213","request_id":"req_011CfCdXxhZAfPExmHrWK69g"}
