{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCdXyAMJJQkSU4eQtCwU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WMAKvi3LxaDPZpK6sqH439","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && cat >> research/ROUNDS.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Round 6 RESULT (agent-6, 2733 s)\n| cand | recipe | score |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | R3 + potential-based progress shaping (memory) | 0.4131 |\n| 1 | R3 - `lat_mid` | 0.4365 |\n\n**Conclusions**\n- H11 refuted (-0.147): even a *zero-net-mass*, policy-invariant potential term loses badly.\n- H12 refuted (-0.124): removing a single 0.5-max dense term also loses badly.\n- 12 recipes measured. R3 = 0.5605; **everything else lies in [0.361, 0.511]**. Removals hurt as much\n  as additions, and a policy-invariant shaping term hurts as much as a structural one. That pattern is\n  not what a smooth reward-design landscape looks like - it is what a **chaotic recipe -> score map**\n  looks like (single seed, single 50-epoch run, sigma ~ 0.04).\n\n### Pivot: measure the noise directly\n`selected_epoch` is an explicit design variable (1..50) and changing it does **not** change training at\nall - same recipe, same seed, same trajectory, only a different checkpoint is evaluated. So submitting\nR3 at two other epochs is a *pure, uncontaminated* measurement of how much of the 0.44-0.56 spread is\nlate-training wobble rather than reward structure.\n\n---\n## Round 7\n* **H13 (candidate_0)** R3 @ `selected_epoch = 48`\n* **H14 (candidate_1)** R3 @ `selected_epoch = 44`\n\nIf both land near 0.56, the recipe differences measured so far are real structure and R3 is a genuine\noptimum. If they scatter over ~0.45-0.60, then late-epoch wobble dominates, epoch choice is itself a\nfirst-class lever, and the right move is to scan it.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nbase = json.load(open('/workspace/research/best/r3_bottom_0.5605.json'))\nfor ep, path in ((48, '/workspace/reward.json'), (44, '/workspace/candidates/reward_1.json')):\n    r = json.loads(json.dumps(base)); r['selected_epoch'] = ep\n    open(path, 'w').write(json.dumps(r, separators=(',', ': '), indent=1) + \"\\n\")\nEOF\n/usr/local/bin/validate-reward --json /workspace/reward.json && /usr/local/bin/validate-reward --json /workspace/candidates/reward_1.json && rsi-submit 2>&1 | tail -20","description":"Submit round 7: epoch-selection probe","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":591,"cache_creation_input_tokens":540,"cache_read_input_tokens":212204,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":540},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f43d26ba-365d-4aca-85d2-d7eee3bfb38e","uuid":"0ff50a28-2c19-4454-b661-b9647e5d1a57","request_id":"req_011CfCdXxhZAfPExmHrWK69g"}
