{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCh4MuG2XrHDT84LKsWw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015tBZogozYRsmGSbDhCJ4QQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && cat >> research/ROUNDS.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Round 7 RESULT (agent-7, 2727 s) - the noise measurement\n| epoch | score |\n|---|---|\n| 44 | 0.5547 |\n| 48 | 0.5557 |\n| 50 | 0.5605 (round 3) |\n\n**Spread = 0.006 over 6 epochs / 98k transitions.** Late training is converged and stable.\n- `selected_epoch` is *not* a lever - keep 50.\n- More importantly: the 0.36-0.56 spread between recipes is **real reward structure**, not\n  checkpoint wobble. The designed staircase 0.378 -> 0.394 -> 0.465 -> 0.561 is signal.\n- So R3 is a genuine, narrow optimum. Every *structural* addition/removal tried has been downhill.\n  What has never been tried: **small parameter moves within R3's proven form.**\n  The two wins (depth ramp, bottoming term) were both of exactly one form:\n  **reward mass on the `dz` axis inside the bore, laterally gated.** Tune that, change nothing else.\n\n---\n## Round 8\nPure shape test of the in-bore ramp, with the endpoints held fixed (0 at the mouth, 2.0 at the\nbottom) so the peak reward is unchanged - the only thing that moves is *where inside the bore the\nreward mass sits*.\n\n* **H15 (candidate_0)** `depth -> sqrt(depth)` (concave): pays much more for the *first* millimetres\n  of entry (0.69 instead of 0.24 at 2.5 mm in), which is the hardest sub-task.\n* **H16 (candidate_1)** `depth -> depth^2` (convex): pays more only once the peg is already deep.\n\nR3's linear ramp = 0.5605 is the control.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nbase = json.load(open('/workspace/research/best/r3_bottom_0.5605.json'))\nfor op, nid, path in ((\"sqrt\",\"depth_s\",\"/workspace/reward.json\"),\n                      (\"square\",\"depth_q\",\"/workspace/candidates/reward_1.json\")):\n    r = json.loads(json.dumps(base)); n = r['nodes']\n    i = next(k for k, x in enumerate(n) if x['id'] == 'depth_bonus')\n    n.insert(i, {\"id\": nid, \"op\": op, \"args\": [\"depth\"]})\n    n[i+1]['args'] = [\"w_depth\", nid, \"gate\"]\n    open(path, 'w').write(json.dumps(r, separators=(',', ': '), indent=1) + \"\\n\")\nEOF\n/usr/local/bin/validate-reward --json /workspace/reward.json && /usr/local/bin/validate-reward --json /workspace/candidates/reward_1.json && cd research && python3 probe.py /workspace/reward.json /workspace/candidates/reward_1.json 2>&1 | grep -E \"dz.dxy|^ +(0.0|5.0|15.0|22.0|25.0) \" ","description":"Build, validate, probe round-8 shape variants"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":459,"cache_creation_input_tokens":628,"cache_read_input_tokens":216559,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":628},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f43d26ba-365d-4aca-85d2-d7eee3bfb38e","uuid":"d8df28c6-f187-4fc0-bac2-36c6a431aa91","request_id":"req_011CfCh4Lwi8JSWjaTFHHLbM"}
