{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCkcz9pnCLgLiywUWLP4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fsc4WfdCuPqr3SpwTtYMaR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && cat >> research/ROUNDS.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Round 8 RESULT (agent-8, 2709 s)\n| cand | in-bore ramp shape | score |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | `sqrt(depth)` concave | 0.4561 |\n| 1 | `depth^2` convex | 0.4463 |\n| - | `depth` linear (R3) | **0.5605** |\n\n**Conclusions**\n- H15 and H16 both refuted (-0.104, -0.114) even though the endpoints were held identical.\n  A *linear* in-bore ramp beats both curvatures by a wide margin.\n- Noise accounting: 14 distinct training runs so far, mean 0.443, sd 0.055; R3 is +2.1 sd.\n  Every perturbation - large or small, additive or subtractive - lands in 0.36-0.51.\n  Best model of the data: **real signal from the in-bore `dz` terms (baseline 0.378 -> R2 0.465 is\n  +0.087 and survives any noise model), plus per-run trajectory noise of sd ~0.05.**\n  Round 7 rules out *checkpoint* noise, not *trajectory* noise.\n- Consequence: only changes with a large true effect can be detected, and the one axis with a\n  demonstrated large true effect is the laterally-gated in-bore `dz` reward. Round 4 confounded two\n  additions on that axis; separate them.\n\n---\n## Round 9\n* **H17 (candidate_0)** R3 + `3.0*squash(dz,250,0)*gate` **alone** (the mid-scale rung of the round-4\n  ladder, without the ultra-peaky `squash(dz,3000,0)`). Round 4 bundled them; if the ultra-peaky term\n  was the poison (a 0.44 mm-wide spike the critic cannot represent), the mid rung alone should behave\n  like R3's bottoming term did, which added +1.5 of mass and gained +0.096.\n* **H18 (candidate_1)** R3 with the in-bore block scaled x1.3 as a pure **gain** change\n  (`w_depth 2.0 -> 2.6`, `w_bottom 3.0 -> 3.9`): no new scales, no shape change.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nbase = json.load(open('/workspace/research/best/r3_bottom_0.5605.json'))\n\nr = json.loads(json.dumps(base)); n = r['nodes']\ni = next(k for k, x in enumerate(n) if x['id'] == 'shaping')\nfor node in [{\"id\":\"zmid\",\"op\":\"keypoint_squash\",\"args\":[\"dz\"],\"a\":250.0,\"b\":0.0},\n             {\"id\":\"w_zmid\",\"op\":\"const\",\"args\":[],\"value\":3.0},\n             {\"id\":\"zmid_bonus\",\"op\":\"mul\",\"args\":[\"w_zmid\",\"zmid\",\"gate\"]}]:\n    n.insert(i, node); i += 1\nn[-1]['args'] = [\"shaping\",\"depth_bonus\",\"zmid_bonus\",\"bottom_bonus\",\"engaged\",\"success\"]\nopen('/workspace/reward.json','w').write(json.dumps(r, separators=(',', ': '), indent=1)+\"\\n\")\n\nr = json.loads(json.dumps(base))\nfor x in r['nodes']:\n    if x['id'] == 'w_depth': x['value'] = 2.6\n    if x['id'] == 'w_bottom': x['value'] = 3.9\nopen('/workspace/candidates/reward_1.json','w').write(json.dumps(r, separators=(',', ': '), indent=1)+\"\\n\")\nEOF\n/usr/local/bin/validate-reward --json /workspace/reward.json && /usr/local/bin/validate-reward --json /workspace/candidates/reward_1.json && rsi-submit 2>&1 | tail -20","description":"Submit round 9","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":596,"cache_creation_input_tokens":544,"cache_read_input_tokens":224850,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":544},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f43d26ba-365d-4aca-85d2-d7eee3bfb38e","uuid":"f85bc491-356a-4432-a0d4-2066b25094a2","request_id":"req_011CfCkcyf4HSExYs5QNgTB2"}
