{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCpAkbV5V8J62iRwTMbX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0161AQ9wtQYYRo8yDtkSZsPg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && cat >> research/ROUNDS.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Round 9 RESULT (agent-9, 2710 s)\n| cand | recipe | score |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0 | R3 + `3.0*sq(dz,250)*gate` alone (mid rung only) | 0.4443 |\n| 1 | R3 with in-bore block x1.3 (pure gain) | 0.5010 |\n\n- H17 refuted (-0.116): the mid rung alone is just as bad as the full ladder, so round 4's loss was\n  not caused by the ultra-peaky 0.44 mm term specifically.\n- H18 refuted (-0.060): even a **pure 30% gain change**, with no new terms, no new scales and no\n  shape change, costs 0.06.\n\n16 distinct training runs: mean 0.449, sd 0.050. R3 (0.5605) is +2.22 sd; the expected max of 16\nnoise draws is +1.77 sd. A 30% gain tweak losing 0.06 is not plausible reward-design physics.\n\n---\n## Round 10 - the decisive experiment\nEverything hinges on one question that no experiment so far can answer: **is the recipe -> score map\nsmooth (so R3 is real structure and my 9 refutations are real), or chaotic (so R3 is a lucky\ntrajectory and the refutations are noise)?**\n\nTest it with perturbations too small to be a reward-design change at all:\n\n* **H19 (candidate_0)** R3 with `w_bottom 3.0 -> 3.001` (+0.03%).\n* **H20 (candidate_1)** R3 with `w_depth 2.0 -> 2.001` (+0.05%).\n\nThese change the per-step reward by <1e-3 - far below anything a policy could care about, but far\nabove fp32 epsilon, so the gradients differ and the 6,400-step trajectory can diverge.\n\n**Prediction under \"smooth\":** both return 0.5605 +- 0.01, and I should stop perturbing R3.\n**Prediction under \"chaotic\":** they scatter over 0.42-0.56, which means sd ~0.05 of trajectory noise\nis the dominant term in every comparison I have made, and the right strategy becomes drawing more\nsamples from the good-structure family rather than redesigning it.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nbase = json.load(open('/workspace/research/best/r3_bottom_0.5605.json'))\nfor nid, val, path in (('w_bottom', 3.001, '/workspace/reward.json'),\n                       ('w_depth',  2.001, '/workspace/candidates/reward_1.json')):\n    r = json.loads(json.dumps(base))\n    for x in r['nodes']:\n        if x['id'] == nid: x['value'] = val\n    open(path, 'w').write(json.dumps(r, separators=(',', ': '), indent=1) + \"\\n\")\nEOF\n/usr/local/bin/validate-reward --json /workspace/reward.json && /usr/local/bin/validate-reward --json /workspace/candidates/reward_1.json && rsi-submit 2>&1 | tail -20","description":"Submit round 10: chaos probe","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":469,"cache_creation_input_tokens":626,"cache_read_input_tokens":232080,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":626},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f43d26ba-365d-4aca-85d2-d7eee3bfb38e","uuid":"4babb789-9ce7-4640-a10c-ff507e4f1141","request_id":"req_011CfCpAjwYmFqBjvSBCpGdG"}
