{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCsmj9zTxmHhD6Kb1WNX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A crucial detail in the logs: R3 at epochs 50/48/44 all show mean return `213.35773` — identical training, bitwise reproducible. The two micro-variants diverged to returns of 233 and 241 — **higher reward but lower success**."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3820,"cache_read_input_tokens":238266,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3820},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f43d26ba-365d-4aca-85d2-d7eee3bfb38e","uuid":"20e3283b-d221-48ab-b4a6-c679eaf4cffe","request_id":"req_011CfCsmigxigmUW14BY7Epg"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCsmj9zTxmHhD6Kb1WNX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MDFRi741BKpkukoMZpGAGb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> research/ROUNDS.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Round 10 RESULT (agent-10, 2730 s) - DECISIVE\n| cand | change vs R3 | score | final mean return |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| - | none (R3, epochs 50/48/44) | 0.5605 / 0.5557 / 0.5547 | 213.35773 (identical all three) |\n| 0 | `w_bottom 3.0 -> 3.001` (+0.03%) | 0.5059 | 233.15 |\n| 1 | `w_depth 2.0 -> 2.001` (+0.05%) | 0.5195 | 241.30 |\n\n**The map is chaotic.** Two facts pin this down:\n1. R3 submitted three times reproduces the mean return to all 8 printed digits - training is\n   bitwise deterministic, so nothing here is evaluation noise.\n2. Changing one constant by 0.03% - a reward difference of <1e-3 per step, which no policy could\n   care about - moves terminal success by **-0.055**, and moves the *final mean return* by +9%.\n\nSo a single 50-epoch run has trajectory noise of sd ~0.03-0.05 in terminal success, and **every\nsingle-draw comparison in rounds 1-9 was dominated by it.** What survives:\n- The **R3 family** (4 draws: 0.5605, 0.5195, 0.5059, and 0.5010 for the x1.3 gain) has mean ~0.52.\n  The baseline is 0.378. **The in-bore, laterally-gated `dz` reward is worth ~+0.14 of real signal.**\n- Effects smaller than ~0.10 in a single draw (i.e. H6, H9, H12, H15-H18) are simply not measurable\n  at this budget and should not be reported as refuted mechanisms.\n\n**New actionable signal:** across the three R3-family runs, *higher* mean return went with *lower*\nsuccess (213 -> 0.561, 233 -> 0.506, 241 -> 0.520). The diverged policies earn more reward while\ninserting less. That is reward misalignment with a specific address: the reward pays ~3.1/step for\nsitting **partially** inserted (engaged, dz~15 mm) versus 7.1/step for bottoming out, and a full\n1.0/step of that partial payment is the flat `engaged` bonus earned after only 2.5 mm of entry.\n\n---\n## Round 11\nAttack that misalignment directly - shift payment from partial insertion to full insertion, keeping\nR3's structure and total scale otherwise intact.\n\n* **H21 (candidate_0)** `engaged` 1.0 -> 0.6: stop paying a full unit for 2.5 mm of entry\n  (partial/full ratio 2.30 -> 2.55).\n* **H22 (candidate_1)** `success` 1.0 -> 1.6: pay more for the state the evaluation actually scores\n  (partial/full ratio 2.30 -> 2.62).\n\nGiven sd ~0.04, each is also an independent draw from the best-known family; only a swing >0.10\nshould be read as mechanism rather than noise.\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nbase = json.load(open('/workspace/research/best/r3_bottom_0.5605.json'))\ndef weighted(path, term, w):\n    r = json.loads(json.dumps(base)); n = r['nodes']\n    i = len(n) - 1\n    n.insert(i, {\"id\": \"w_\" + term, \"op\": \"const\", \"args\": [], \"value\": w})\n    n.insert(i + 1, {\"id\": term + \"_w\", \"op\": \"mul\", \"args\": [\"w_\" + term, term]})\n    n[-1]['args'] = [term + \"_w\" if a == term else a for a in n[-1]['args']]\n    open(path, 'w').write(json.dumps(r, separators=(',', ': '), indent=1) + \"\\n\")\nweighted('/workspace/reward.json', 'engaged', 0.6)\nweighted('/workspace/candidates/reward_1.json', 'success', 1.6)\nEOF\n/usr/local/bin/validate-reward --json /workspace/reward.json && /usr/local/bin/validate-reward --json /workspace/candidates/reward_1.json && python3 -c \"\nimport json\nfor p in ['/workspace/reward.json','/workspace/candidates/reward_1.json']:\n    print(p, json.load(open(p))['nodes'][-1]['args'])\" && rsi-submit 2>&1 | tail -20","description":"Submit round 11","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3820,"cache_read_input_tokens":238266,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3820},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f43d26ba-365d-4aca-85d2-d7eee3bfb38e","uuid":"6284b3fa-2120-4f60-8a5e-f34055e1ce63","request_id":"req_011CfCsmigxigmUW14BY7Epg"}
