{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfDSKtE4jw5DAhUhFrAmM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Hdqo3nDNceqBR39MhjChee","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && cat >> research/ROUNDS.md <<'EOF'\n\n### Round 20 RESULT (agent-20, 2757 s)\n`c_invbore` 40.2 -> 0.4043 | `c_gate_s` 505 -> 0.4404. Both in-band, no new best.\nFamily draws (15): **mean 0.505, sd 0.052** - the mean keeps regressing as draws accumulate\n(0.526 @ 9 -> 0.518 @ 13 -> 0.505 @ 15), confirming R14's 0.6016 is a ~+2 sd outlier and blind\nresampling is only ~5%/round. Testing a *new* mechanism weakly dominates resampling: same lottery\nodds if its family mean is the same, better odds if it is higher.\n\n---\n## Round 21 - a mechanism the reward is currently blind to: peg tilt\nGeometry: 7.986 mm peg in an 8.100 mm bore = **0.057 mm radial clearance**. A peg inserted to depth\nL two-point jams beyond a tilt of about `2*0.057/L` - only **0.33 deg at 20 mm depth**.\nThe policy cannot command roll/pitch (the controller forces the fingertip target upright), but tilt\narises from contact compliance, and the policy *can* learn not to push laterally while deep.\n\nMeasured blindness of the current reward at the bottomed pose (dxy=0, dz=0.5 mm):\n\n| peg tilt | 0.0 deg | 0.3 deg | 1 deg | 5 deg |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| R14 reward | 6.954 | 6.954 | 6.952 | 6.907 |\n\nA 5 deg tilt costs 0.047 out of 6.95. `keypoint_distance` does encode tilt, but only 0.05*theta in\nmetres - 0.28 mm at the jamming angle, which all three squash terms read as essentially zero.\n\nFix: multiply the in-bore block by `sech(a * sin(tilt/2))`, computed from the peg quaternion as\n`sqrt(qx^2+qy^2)`. **The maximum reward is unchanged** (a vertical, bottomed peg still scores 6.954),\nso this adds no reward mass - the property that has survived best in this study.\n\n* **H25 (candidate_0)** `a = 150` (half-width 1.0 deg) -> 0.3 deg costs 3%, 1 deg costs 24%.\n* **H26 (candidate_1)** `a = 300` (half-width 0.5 deg) -> 0.3 deg costs 12%, 1 deg costs 41%.\n\nGiven sd 0.052, only a swing >0.10 is readable; two draws on the same new mechanism double the\nchance of seeing it if it is real.\nEOF\nrsi-submit 2>&1 | tail -8","description":"Submit round 21","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6925,"cache_read_input_tokens":290991,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6925},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f43d26ba-365d-4aca-85d2-d7eee3bfb38e","uuid":"63234c13-87ed-4394-aa11-821fa34db5ab","request_id":"req_011CfDSKsWQeP4v1vhJShaHU"}
